  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_rose_gall_cb256732a97f1ef3ff865f39a33dea13b67b7cbb1d6fde8175ce84263d54e75db2">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a gall produced by a gall wasp on a rose plant; especially a robin’s pincushion or bedeguar [A moss-like excrescence on rose-bushes: it is a kind of gall produced by the puncture of a small insect Cynips rosæ: OED s.v. bedeguar, used by apothecaries, 1st use 1578] (OED s.v. rose gall n.)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
